  "geometryBasis": "The mapped museum exterior and measured roof return derive the long 399 m mapped envelope within the institution’s published 404 m construction length. The building follows a surveyed bearing. Way-level geometry fixes the curved glass part, northern volumes, pond and two pavilions.",
  "sectionBasis": "The architect describes the long fortress-wall composition and an open covered square between the east and west wings. The institution records a 43.08 m maximum and the stepped entrance. Its award schedule specifies dressed granite, aluminum paneling, flat slabs and low-emissivity glazing.",
  "limitations": [
    "The building’s dimensions and open central plaza follow the museum’s published description and mapped outline. Partition locations, facade bay rhythms, open-plaza soffit details and small roof levels are estimated.",
    "Thirty-metre Copernicus radar returns corroborate the higher eastern and central wings and lower northern structures. Precise heights, the attachment point for the published maximum and stair landings are approximate. The higher portions are narrow, since the 30 m cells average roof and open space.",
    "The Celadon and Bosingak exterior pavilions retain their mapped footprints. Decorative framing, surface design and lower corner details are generalized."
